The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog. Pack my box with five dozen
liquor jugs. How vexingly quick daft zebras jump! The five boxing wizards
jump quickly. Sphinx of black quartz, judge my vow. Two driven jocks help
fax my big quiz. Five quacking zephyrs jolt my wax bed. The job requires
extra pluck and zeal from every young wage earner.

We study the typographic fidelity of a Typst reimplementation of the acmart
document class. The goal is for idiomatic Typst source to render as closely
as possible to the equivalent LaTeX output, matching fonts, sizes, margins,
and inter-line spacing. This paragraph exists purely to fill several lines so
that line height and justification can be compared between the two engines.

A third paragraph continues the comparison. Notice that the first line of each
paragraph is indented, that paragraphs are set solid with no extra vertical
space between them, and that the text is justified to both margins. The body
font is Libertinus Serif at ten points, set on a twelve point baseline.

